# Tripp-light (Tripp Lite SRCOOL)

Home Assistant **custom integration** for the Tripp Lite **SRCOOLNET** SNMP Webcard Interface Module over Telnet.

## Supported hardware

- **Required adapter:** [Tripp Lite SRCOOLNET](https://tripplite.eaton.com/snmp-webcard-interface-module-remote-cooling-management-srcool12k-srxcool12k~SRCOOLNET) — SNMP Webcard Interface Module for Remote Cooling Management (SRCOOL12K / SRXCOOL12K).
- **Not supported:** Direct telnet to SRCOOL units without the SRCOOLNET adapter. Do **not** document or imply support for SRCOOLNETLX or generic SR(X)COOL units.
- User-facing docs (`README.md`, `translations/en.json`) must name **SRCOOLNET** and link to the Eaton product page above.

## Distribution

- **Canonical GitHub repo:** [Shaffer-Softworks/Tripp-light](https://github.com/Shaffer-Softworks/Tripp-light) (case-sensitive; use this name in `hacs/default` PRs).
- **HACS default inclusion:** open PR [hacs/default#7959](https://github.com/hacs/default/pull/7959) via fork `sickkick/HACS` branch `add-tripp-lite-srcool`. See `.cursor/rules/hacs-default-pr.mdc`.
- Until merged: users add via HACS → Integrations → Custom repositories → URL `https://github.com/Shaffer-Softworks/Tripp-light`, category **Integration**.

## Repository layout

```
hacs.json                          # HACS manifest (root only)
mypy.ini                           # mypy config for CI
pytest.ini                         # pytest config
README.md, icon.png                # README art; source for brand/ assets
.github/workflows/ci.yml
tests/                             # pytest suite
custom_components/tripp_lite_srcool/
  __init__.py, manifest.json
  brand/                           # HA 2026.3+ local brand images (see below)
  config_flow.py, connection.py, const.py
  climate.py, sensor.py, binary_sensor.py, switch.py
  srcool_telnet.py
  translations/en.json
```

- All integration code under `custom_components/tripp_lite_srcool/` — never at repo root.
- Domain: `tripp_lite_srcool` (`const.py`).
- Platforms: `binary_sensor`, `climate`, `sensor`, `switch` via `async_forward_entry_setups` in `__init__.py` — **not** in `manifest.json`.

## manifest.json (hassfest)

- Keys: `domain`, `name`, then **alphabetically** (`codeowners`, `config_flow`, `documentation`, `iot_class`, `issue_tracker`, `requirements`, `version`).
- **Do not** include `icon` or `platforms` — hassfest rejects them for integrations.
- Bump `version` on each release (currently **0.6.0**).
- **`requirements`:** `telnetlib3>=4.0.0` (replaces stdlib `telnetlib`, removed in Python 3.13).

## Brand images (`brand/`)

- Home Assistant **2026.3+** loads `custom_components/tripp_lite_srcool/brand/` automatically.
- Required sizes (PNG): `icon.png` 256×256, `icon@2x.png` 512×512; optional `logo.png` / `logo@2x.png`.
- Regenerate from repo root `icon.png` (1024×1024) with `sips -z`.
- Do **not** put `icon` in `manifest.json`; entity icons use `mdi:*` in platform code.

## Device behavior (critical)

The SRCOOL telnet interface is **flaky**:

- Does **not** tolerate frequent polling or overlapping telnet traffic.
- **One session** at a time — config flow must not leave a second connection open.

Do not add per-entity polling or `async_request_refresh()` after climate writes.

## Connection & polling (v0.6.0+)

| Concern | Pattern |
|--------|---------|
| Telnet library | **telnetlib3** async (`open_connection` + reader/writer) |
| Serialize I/O | `asyncio.Lock` per client + per-host lock via `get_host_lock()` in `connection.py` |
| One session | Single `SRCOOLClient` per config entry in `hass.data`; host lock prevents config-flow overlap |
| Poll interval | `SCAN_INTERVAL = 60` in `const.py` |
| Diagnostics fetch | `include_diagnostics=True` on first poll + every `DIAGNOSTICS_REFRESH_INTERVAL` (3600s); telnet menu `5` |
| Diagnostics persist | On polls **without** fetch, copy `DIAGNOSTIC_KEYS` from `coordinator.data` into the new result — `get_status()` omits those keys when `include_diagnostics=False` |
| Config validation | `async_validate_connection()` in `connection.py`: unchanged creds → `check_connection()` on live session; changed creds → disconnect live → temp `verify_connection()` → restore on failure |
| Unload | `await client.disconnect()` in `async_unload_entry` |
| Climate writes | Direct `await client.*` (no executor); optimistic `coordinator.async_set_updated_data()`; no immediate refresh |
| Startup | No `update_before_add`; one `async_config_entry_first_refresh()` |
| Device registry | `identifiers={(DOMAIN, port_name)}` on climate + sensors |

## Diagnostics (sensors + coordinator)

- **Keys** in `const.py` → `DIAGNOSTIC_KEYS` (frozenset): telnet menu `5` fields preserved hourly between fetches.
- **Keys** in `const.py` → `DIAGNOSTIC_ENTITY_KEYS`: `dehumidifying_status` — hidden sensor redundant with **Dehumidify Mode** switch.
- **Sensors** (`sensor.py`): `DIAGNOSTIC_KEYS | DIAGNOSTIC_ENTITY_KEYS` use `EntityCategory.DIAGNOSTIC`.
- **Telnet**: `_get_diagnostics_unlocked()` — main menu → `5`; parsed in `srcool_telnet.py`. Failures log `Error fetching diagnostics` and must not wipe cached values.
- **Bug (v0.5.3)**: coordinator replaced full `data` every 60s without diagnostic keys → entities showed **Unknown** after the first minute. **Fix (v0.5.4+)**: preserve `DIAGNOSTIC_KEYS` in `__init__.py` `_async_update` when `include_diagnostics` is false.

## Telnet menu paths (`srcool_telnet.py`)

- Status: `M` → `1` → `1`
- Identification: `M` → `1` → `2` (device info + serial)
- Preferences: `M` → `1` → `5` (committed setpoint, dehumidifying status, units)
- Setpoint **read**: Preferences `Set Point Temperature` only (v0.5.9+ — do not poll Controls edit screen; staged values caused desync)
- Setpoint **write**: `M` → `1` → `3` → `2` → `1` → value → **E** → **Y**
- Fan **write**: `M` → `1` → `3` → `4` → `1` → value → **E** → **Y** (control codes: `0`=auto, `1`=low, `2`=medium, `3`=high)
- Dehumidify write: `M` → `1` → `5` → `1` → `1` or `2`
- Shutdown: `M` → `1` → `3` → `3` → `Y` (confirm only — no `E`)
- Diagnostics: main menu `5` (poll rarely; see **Diagnostics** above)
- **No telnet power-on** — Controls `1` is Reboot SNMP Card; climate COOL write is ignored
- Every navigation/write step: `readuntil(PROMPT_READY)`; return `M` after control writes

### Control Data commit (v0.5.8+)

Setpoint and fan edits are **two-step** on the SNMP card: enter value on edit screen, then **Execute (`E`)** → **Yes (`Y`)** to reach the physical unit. Without E+Y, Control Data table updates but Preferences / status lag.

## Fan mode (v0.5.10)

**Symptom (2026-06-12):** Climate fan mode never shows `high`; history cycles `low` ↔ `medium` only.

**Root cause:** Unit was in **Auto fan** (`Auto Fan Speed: On`, control data `0`). In auto mode the status screen `Fan Speed` field reports the **actual running speed** (varies low/medium with load), not the commanded mode. Integration read that field directly → climate card showed `low`/`medium`, never `auto` or `high`.

**Fix (v0.5.10):** When `auto_fan == "on"`, set coordinator `fan` to `"auto"`. Climate optimistic writes also set `auto_fan` on/off. Normalize device label `Med` → `medium` (`FAN_SPEED_ALIASES`).

**Behavior notes:**

- Status `Fan Speed` lags ~5s behind a manual speed change (physical ramp).
- `high` **does** commit when selected (verified live on `10.10.0.61`); user must leave Auto and pick High explicitly.
- `sensor.srcool_auto_fan` entity id: `sensor.srcool_auto_fan` (not `sensor.srcool_auto_fan_speed`).

## Session desync & parsing (v0.5.7)

**Symptom (2026-05-25):** HA logs every 60s: `Could not parse Fan Speed in status screen` + `Could not parse target_temp from screen`. Fan sensor → `unknown`, operating mode → `off`, climate → `off` while unit still cooling. **Reload integration** fixes until desync again.

**Root cause:** Stale telnet session reads the **wrong screen** (Devices menu or Controls menu) instead of Status / Set Point. Those screens lack `Fan Speed`, `Return Air Temperature`, and `Value:` — parsers fail; missing `Operating Mode` defaults to `"off"`.

**Screen markers** (`srcool_telnet.py`):

| Screen | Marker / validation |
|--------|---------------------|
| Status | `STATUS_SCREEN_MARKER = "Device Status Menu"` |
| Set point | `SETPOINT_SCREEN_MARKER = "Temperature (F)"` |

**Recovery (v0.5.7+):** `_get_status_unlocked()` → up to 2 attempts: validate screens in `_fetch_status_screens_unlocked()` / setpoint step; on failure `disconnect()` and retry. Raises `ConnectionError` if both fail (coordinator keeps old data per `__init__.py`).

**Parsers:**

- Fan: `_parse_fan_speed()` — regex `Fan Speed\s*:`; skip lines starting with `Auto Fan`; then `_normalize_fan_speed()`. If `auto_fan` is on, `fan` is forced to `"auto"` (v0.5.10).
- Target temp: `_parse_target_temp()` reads `Set Point Temperature` from Preferences (`prefs_raw`) only.

**Do not** open a second telnet client to the SRCOOLNET card while HA is polling.

**Debug on user HA:** MCP `ha_get_logs` source `system`/`error_log` search `tripp_lite_srcool`; entities `sensor.srcool_fan_speed`, `sensor.srcool_auto_fan`, `sensor.srcool_operating_mode`, `climate.climate_control_tripp_lite_srcool`. User unit: `10.10.0.61`, config entry `SRCOOL 10.10.0.61`, currently **v0.6.0**.

**Live verify (read-only):** from repo root, `await SRCOOLClient(host, 23, ...).get_status()` against `10.10.0.61`; stress-test 25 polls; desync test: leave session on Devices menu then call `get_status()` — should auto-recover.

## CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`)

Python **3.11** and **3.13** on `ubuntu-latest`:

1. `isort --check-only custom_components tests`
2. `flake8 custom_components tests` (max line length **79** — E501)
3. `mypy custom_components` (uses root `mypy.ini`)
4. `pytest tests/`
5. `home-assistant/actions/hassfest@master` — **not** bare `hassfest` CLI
6. `hacs/action@main` with `category: integration`

### mypy.ini

- `follow_imports = skip`, `disable_error_code = import-untyped`
- `tripp_lite_srcool.config_flow`: `disable_error_code = call-arg` for `domain=DOMAIN`

### HACS GitHub repo requirements (not in code)

Forks must set on GitHub or HACS validation fails:

- **Description** (e.g. “Home Assistant custom integration for Tripp Lite SRCOOLNET Remote Cooling Management over Telnet.”)
- **Topics:** `home-assistant`, `homeassistant`, `hacs`, `hacs-integration`

## When changing the integration

1. Bump `manifest.json` `version`.
2. Keep `issue_tracker` / `documentation` URLs in sync with GitHub.
3. Translations: `translations/en.json` only.
4. Style: single quotes in `const.py`; run `isort` + `flake8` + `pytest` before push.

## Out of scope unless requested

- New or duplicate PRs to `hacs/default` (one open: #7959)
- PR to `home-assistant/brands` (local `brand/` preferred for custom repo)
